- rule 5: keep the sky dim: The top third's brightness, left to right: 0.31, 0.29, 0.28 (limit 0.36).
- rule 6: lit from below: The bottom of two gates and the wall between is 0.25 warmer than its top, on a scale where 0 is the same colour and 1 is pure red against pure blue; it needs 0.10 (the reference measures about 0.17).
- rule 5: no burnt-out colour: Nothing apart from tiny highlights is at its colour limit.
- main rule: every strong thing points at the same place: where the lines meet 0.50 across, 0.50 down; centre of the brightest parts 0.58 across, 0.50 down; centre of the warm light 0.64 across, 0.52 down; centre of the story props 0.47 across, 0.60 down; centre of two gates and the wall between 0.50 across, 0.59 down. Together they span 0.17 of the frame wide and 0.10 tall (limit 0.40 x 0.50, holding two gates and the wall between).

